\pard\nowidctlpar\cf1\b\f0\fs18\lang1033 SQLAgain\b0  is a Tool to run a File containing Oracle SQL Statements against multiple Oracle Databases using SQL*Plus.\par
\par
You drag and drop a .sql File from Explorer to the SQLAgain icon or application,\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720 select one or more Databases, \par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}an Oracle Schema for the Database Connection \par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}press either \par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li1080\b\i Execute \b0\i0 to run the File in Foreground or \par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}\b\i Schedule \b0\i0 to run it later - \par

\pard\nowidctlpar and get a cup of tea or coffe. \par
Your done. \par
Let SQLAgain do the repetitive connect to the next database and run the same file again and again, until the end of the database list is processed.\par
\par
\b\lang2055 Prerequisites\par

\pard{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\b0\lang1033 Oracles SQL*Plus \endash  from a Oracle DB, Oracle Client or Oracle Instant Client \par
{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}tnsnames.ora \endash  the well-known configuration file used by Oracle databases.\par

\pard{\*\pn\pnlvlcont\pnf4\pnindent0{\pntxtb\'B7}}\nowidctlpar\highlight2\b\par
\highlight0\b0\f1\par
\b\f0 Schedule SQL - delay execution\b0\par
In addition to a normal execution in \i foreground\i0 , you may schedule your prepared SQL job later - when the time is right for the long running delete, alter or update statements or when the maintenance window is open for the change of the data structure.\line SQLAgain lets you create a Windows Scheduler Task, sends an E-mail confirmation including a Calendar Event; executes the SQL statements and finally sends its output by E-mail to your inbox.\par
