{\pntext\f4\'B7\tab}\b SQLPATH\line\b0 SQL*Plus searches for SQL scripts, including login.sql/glogin.sql, in the current directory and then in the directories specified by SQLPATH, and in the subdirectories of SQLPATH directories. SQLPATH is a colon-separated list of directories. \line SQLAgain sets the directory name of your .sql or .pls file as first directory in SQLPATH - hence your file may start further files without the need to qualify the full path.\line\par
